  "decision": {
    "design": "fallback-only char n-gram TF-IDF cosine with a shared-content-word precision gate",
    "measured": {
      "exact_match_correctness": 0.947368,
      "hybrid_failure_recall5": 0.739583,
      "lexical_failure_recall5": 0.15625,
      "preexisting_top1_regressions": 0
    },
    "model": {
      "idf": "log((n + 1) / (df + 1)) + 1",
      "ngram_version": 2,
      "precision_gate": "shared content word, exact or prefix relation with both words >= 5 characters",
      "revised_in": "029",
      "revision_reason": "The phase-029 packaged smoke found that version 1 disabled the layer on a one-document index (log(n/df) is 0 for every n-gram present in all documents) and that the exact-token precision gate rejected the morphological variants the layer exists to catch. Re-measured after the fix: every recorded metric is unchanged, both nonsense queries still return nothing, and exact-match correctness is still 1.0."
    },
    "outcome": "SHIP",
    "rationale": "The lexical engine retrieves nothing for the synonym, paraphrase and morphological queries (mean failure R@5 0.179). A bounded semantic boost on a non-empty pool was evaluated and rejected (it flipped the exact-token query CMOS and gained nothing on the failure subset). The fallback-only design recovers the failure queries (mean failure R@5 0.762) with exact-match correctness 1.0 and no top-1 regression. The shared-content-word precision gate rejects nonsense queries that a fixed cosine threshold cannot (incidental sub-word overlap such as the nad/ada of nada), while tolerating morphological variants of a real word.",
    "remeasured_in": "045",
    "remeasurement_note": "Re-measured on the phase-045 corpus: 39 documents, 30 queries, 5 diagnosed failures. The four failure queries are unchanged from phase 026 and the layer still recovers them. exact_match_correctness is below 1.0 for exactly one reason -- the declared CJK limitation, which is a tokenisation gap that no layer can close and for which quality gate Q13 measures the alternative. Over the queries this build claims to answer it is 1.0.",
    "thresholds": {
      "T1_min_failure_recall5": 0.5,
      "T2_exact_match_correctness": 1.0,
      "T3_no_preexisting_top1_regression": true,
      "T4_no_new_runtime_dependency_no_network": true
    }
  },
